{"id":"u-d619a109-6884-4750-bb83-13c3f9bd3652","src":"community","title":"Push-Pull-Legs (6 Days)","author":"Giovanni .","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/XQYMIb-6-day-ppl-routine","desc":"This program is a highly optimized, 6-day Push/Pull/Legs (PPL) training split designed specifically for maximum muscle hypertrophy while eliminating lower back strain and spinal compression. By strategically removing high-risk compound movements like standard barbell bent-over rows, conventional deadlifts, and forward-leaning low-bar squats, the routine shifts 100% of the mechanical tension directly onto the target muscles.\n\nEvery single workout is streamlined to exactly five exercises to eliminate redundant junk volume, maximize recovery, and ensure high-intensity effort across all working sets.\n\nKey Principles of the Program\n\nAnatomical Alternation: Rather than repeating identical joint angles across the week, the split alternates the physiological focus of each day. Pull days alternate between Lat Width and Upper Back Thickness; Push days alternate between Upper Chest and Lower Chest; and Leg days alternate between a Quad/Adductor focus and a Hamstring/Glute focus.\n\nSynergistic Arm & Shoulder Pairing: Smaller muscle groups are trained efficiently alongside the primary compound lifts that pre-exhaust them. Biceps, forearms, shoulders, and triceps are paired with their exact mechanical counterparts to ensure optimal joint health and structural balance.\n\nProgressive Overload: Each week, add one additional rep per set per exercise and then increase the weight when the maximum rep range is reached.\n\nRep Ranges: 6-10, 8-12, 10-12, 12-15, 15-20.","level":["Novice"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":40,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-11-01T00:25:46.816Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3","Day 4","Day 5","Day 6"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Pull-Up (Assisted)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Suppo